            <div xml:id="d818">

                <pb facs="0907" n="1741" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1741"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/1035</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-31T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1374. For Chadbourne,
                        Smith [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 177. Embassy’s 1577, your No. 169, July 23, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d818-f1"/> The Department has considered wise to allow Cuban
                    authorities to restrict call of Spanish steamers bound from Cuba for Mexican
                    ports and this has now been agreed to by Cuban authorities. Can see no
                    objections to arranging with Spanish Transatlantic and Pinillos Lines to cease
                    their calls to Mexican ports and so soon as you have arranged please cable and
                    we will instruct connecting lines accordingly; also Cuban officials as to
                    transshipments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
